Project Overview
A subscription-based digital services company wants to understand customer behaviour, improve revenue, and reduce customer churn. The project uses Python to clean customer subscription data, perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), create meaningful features, visualize business trends, and build a Linear Regression model to predict customer revenue.

Your dataset contains 2,560 rows and 15 columns, including customer details, subscription plans, monthly fees, tenure, support tickets, session time, discounts, marketing channels, churn status, and total revenue.
Project Implementation Steps
Step 1: Problem Understanding and Dataset Exploration
- Understand the business problem and project objectives.
- Import the required dataset (subscription_data.csv).
- Explore the dataset using Pandas.
- Check the number of rows and columns.
- Examine column names and data types.
- Identify missing values and understand the dataset structure.
Step 2: Data Cleaning Using Pandas
- Identify missing values in Age, City, Average Session Time, and Discount Percentage.
- Handle missing numerical values using median imputation.
- Handle missing categorical values using mode imputation.
- Identify and remove duplicate records.
- Convert Signup Date and Last Active Date into datetime format.
- Identify and handle illogical date records.
- Identify invalid age values (below 18 or above 80).
- Perform final data quality verification.
