Step 6: Data Preparation for Machine Learning
- Select relevant independent variables.
- Select Total Revenue as the target variable.
- Check for missing values in the selected features.
- Remove or handle incomplete records.
- Prepare the feature matrix (X) and target variable (y).
- Split the dataset into training and testing sets using train_test_split().
Step 7: Model Building Using Linear Regression
- Import Linear Regression from Scikit-learn.
- Initialize the Linear Regression model.
- Train the model using training data.
- Predict customer revenue using testing data.
- Compare predicted revenue with actual revenue.
Step 8: Model Evaluation
Evaluate the model using appropriate regression metrics:
- Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
- Mean Squared Error (MSE)
- Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
- R-squared (R²)
These metrics help evaluate how accurately the model predicts customer revenue.
